Klobuchar was the first speaker at [[Inauguration of Joe Biden|Joe Biden's inauguration]] on January 20, 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|date=January 20, 2021|title=Sen. Amy Klobuchar delivers inauguration opening remarks|url=https://www.cnbc.com/video/2021/01/20/sen-amy-klobuchar-delivers-inauguration-opening-remarks.html|website=CNBC|language=en|access-date=January 29, 2021|archive-date=October 16, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016101442/https://www.cnbc.com/video/2021/01/20/sen-amy-klobuchar-delivers-inauguration-opening-remarks.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=January 20, 2021|title=America's 'grit': Amy Klobuchar's full speech at Joe Biden's inauguration|url=https://www.twincities.com/2021/01/20/americas-grit-amy-klobuchars-full-speech-at-joe-bidens-inauguration/|website=Twin Cities|language=en-US|access-date=January 29, 2021|archive-date=October 18, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231018214120/https://www.twincities.com/2021/01/20/americas-grit-amy-klobuchars-full-speech-at-joe-bidens-inauguration/|url-status=live}}</ref>

====Role in the Democratic Party====
[[File:Chuck Schumer greeted UK Prime Minister Sunak at the US Capitol - 2023.jpg|thumb|Klobuchar with [[Chuck Schumer]] and British Prime Minister [[Rishi Sunak]] at the US Capitol, June 7, 2023]]

On March 30, 2008, Klobuchar announced her endorsement of Senator [[Barack Obama]] in the [[2008 Democratic Party presidential primaries|Democratic presidential primary]], promising her [[superdelegate]] vote to him.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.minnpost.com/stories/2008/03/30/1329/klobuchar_to_endorse_obama|title=Klobuchar to endorse Obama|last=Buoen|first=Roger|publisher=MinnPost|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080418051459/http://www.minnpost.com/stories/2008/03/30/1329/klobuchar_to_endorse_obama|archive-date=April 18, 2008|url-status=dead|access-date=March 31, 2008}}</ref> She cited his performance in the Minnesota caucuses, where he won with 66% of the popular vote, as well as her own "independent judgment". In 2016 she was an early supporter of [[Hillary Clinton]]'s second campaign for the Democratic presidential nomination.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.politico.com/story/2014/06/amy-klobuchar-gets-behind-clinton-in-16-107440|title=Klobuchar gets behind Clinton in '16|author=Haberman, Maggie|website=[[Politico]]|date=June 4, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181107083654/https://www.politico.com/story/2014/06/amy-klobuchar-gets-behind-clinton-in-16-107440|archive-date=November 7, 2018|url-status=live|access-date=October 12, 2018}}</ref>

Klobuchar has served as the chair of the [[United States Senate Democratic Steering and Outreach Committee|U.S. Senate Democratic Steering and Outreach Committee]] since 2015.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://news.morris.umn.edu/news/senator-klobuchar-commencement|title = Senator Klobuchar Will Give Commencement Speech|author = Ray, Jenna|website = news.morris.umn.edu|date = March 27, 2018|access-date = June 24, 2019|archive-date = December 26, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221226040904/https://news.morris.umn.edu/news/senator-klobuchar-commencement|url-status = live}}</ref> She became the steering chair of the committee in 2017, with [[Bernie Sanders]] as the outreach chair.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/2016/11/16/senate-democrats-tap-bernie-sanders-lead-outreach/93960822/|title=Senate Democrats tap Bernie Sanders to lead outreach|author=Gaudiano, Nicole|work=USA Today|access-date=June 24, 2019|archive-date=October 17, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231017180006/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/2016/11/16/senate-democrats-tap-bernie-sanders-lead-outreach/93960822/|url-status=live}}</ref> Both represented the Democratic Party in a 2017 televised debate on healthcare policy and the possible repeal of the [[Affordable Care Act]] on [[CNN]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.twincities.com/2017/09/21/amy-klobuchar-bernie-sanders-will-debate-gopers-over-health-care-on-cnn/ | title=Amy Klobuchar, Bernie Sanders will debate GOPers over health care on CNN | last=Stassen-Berger | first=Rachel | date= September 22, 2017| publisher=Twin Cities Pioneer Press | access-date=November 21, 2017 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201035822/http://www.twincities.com/2017/09/21/amy-klobuchar-bernie-sanders-will-debate-gopers-over-health-care-on-cnn/ | archive-date=December 1, 2017 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref>

In 2020, Klobuchar was speculated to be a possible candidate for [[United States Secretary of Agriculture|secretary of agriculture]] or [[United States attorney general]] in the [[Biden administration]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Who Are Contenders for Biden's Cabinet? |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/11/11/us/politics/biden-cabinet.html |access-date=November 11, 2020 |work=The New York Times |date=November 11, 2020 |archive-date=November 11, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201111193928/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/11/11/us/politics/biden-cabinet.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

====Deepfake video====
On July 31, 2025, a [[deepfake]] video of Klobuchar was published on [[Twitter]]<ref name="deepfaketweet">{{cite tweet |author=andy |user=reapingandy |number=1950985354154070289 |date=2025-07-31 |title=🚨BREAKING!!!: Senator Amy Klobuchar of Minnesota weights in on Sydney Sweeney's new American Eagle ad. |access-date=2025-08-22 |link=https://x.com/reapingandy/status/1950985354154070289 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250821183258/https://x.com/reapingandy/status/1950985354154070289 |archive-date=2025-08-21}}</ref> and went viral.<ref name="FortinskyTheHill">{{cite news |last=Fortinsky |first=Sarah |date=2025-08-20 |title=Klobuchar weighs in on deepfake video of her talking about Sydney Sweeney |url=https://thehill.com/blogs/in-the-know/5462605-klobuchar-weighs-in-on-deepfake-video-of-her-talking-about-sydney-sweeney/ |newspaper=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250822001416/https://thehill.com/blogs/in-the-know/5462605-klobuchar-weighs-in-on-deepfake-video-of-her-talking-about-sydney-sweeney/ |archive-date=2025-08-22 |access-date=2025-08-22}}</ref><ref name="HarrisTheWrap">{{cite news |last=Harris |first=Raquel 'Rocky' |date=2025-08-20 |title=Amy Klobuchar Calls for New AI Laws After Sydney Sweeney Deepfake Video Goes Viral: 'It Had Me Saying Vile Things' |url=https://www.thewrap.com/amy-klobuchar-artificial-intelligence-sydney-sweeney-deepfake-video/ |work=[[TheWrap]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250820221629/https://www.thewrap.com/amy-klobuchar-artificial-intelligence-sydney-sweeney-deepfake-video/ |archive-date=2025-08-20 |access-date=2025-08-22}}</ref> The video used footage of a July 30 Senate hearing<ref name="HarrisTheWrap"/><ref name="SwansonCBS">{{cite news |last=Swanson |first=Stephen |date=2025-08-21 |title=Sen. Klobuchar warns of AI's dangers after Sydney Sweeney "deepfake" video surfaces |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/amy-klobuchar-sydney-sweeney-deepfake/ |work=[[CBS News]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250822010116/https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/amy-klobuchar-sydney-sweeney-deepfake/ |archive-date=2025-08-22 |access-date=2025-08-22}}</ref> and purported to show her speaking vulgarly in response to [[Sydney Sweeney Has Great Jeans|American Eagle's July 2025 ad campaign]] involving [[Sydney Sweeney]].<ref name="FortinskyTheHill"/><ref name="HarrisTheWrap"/><ref name="SwansonCBS"/> In a ''[[New York Times]]'' [[op-ed]] on the subject published on August 20,<ref name="deepfakeNYToped">{{cite news |last=Klobuchar |first=Amy |date=2025-08-20 |title=Amy Klobuchar: What I Didn't Say About Sydney Sweeney |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/20/opinion/amy-klobuchar-deepfakes.html |url-access=subscription |newspaper=[[The New York Times]] |url-status=<!--live, but paywalled, ergo leave param blank to prioritize archive--> |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250820200410/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/20/opinion/amy-klobuchar-deepfakes.html |archive-date=2025-08-20 |access-date=2025-08-22}}</ref> Klobuchar wrote that Twitter "refused to take it down or label it" as [[AI-generated]], instead recommending that she try to have a [[Community Note]] added to the tweet.<ref name="HarrisTheWrap"/><ref name="SwansonCBS"/> She implored Congress to pass legislation regulating deepfakes and other AI-generated content.<ref name="FortinskyTheHill"/><ref name="HarrisTheWrap"/>

